ten years the neighbor it's a super  simple supervised machine learning  algorithm that can be solved for both  classification and regression problem  here it's a simple two-dimensional  example for you to have a better  understanding of this algorithm let's  see we wants to classify as a given  point into one of the three groups in  order to find the K nearest neighbors of  the given point we need to calculate the  distance between the given point to the  other points  there are many distance functions but if  you didn't it's the most commonly used  one then we need to sort the nearest  neighbors of the given point by the  distances in increasing order for the  classification problem the point is  classified by a vote of its neighbors  then the point is assigned to the class  most common among its cleaner neighbors  key value here controls the balance  between overfitting and underfitting the  best value can be found with  cross-validation and learning curve a  small p-value ural it leads to low bears  but high variance and a large K or leads  to high bears but low variance it is  important to find a balance between them  for the regression problem we simply  return the average of the K nears the  neighbors labels at the prediction here  it is a simple code example we use a  very famous iris data set and only take  the first two features for demonstration  purpose the cleanest neighbor algorithm  is from s : and it is self explanatory I  encourage you to try it to yourself with  different parameters these two plus a  real visualization from the previous  code example with different K setting  the left part shows the classification  decision boundary with k equal to 15 and  the right plot is for k equal to three  thanks for watching this is a bad-size  ml concept from intuitive Michelini if  you liked this video and want to learn  more make sure to comment like and  subscribe to our Channel see you at the  next one
 

